{title:Waterfall Reprise}
{subtitle:Andrew DeFaria}
{duration:4:13}
{musicpath:Music/Waterfall Reprise.mp3}
{key:D}

{c:Verse 1}

Standing at the edge where the stone gives way,
Mist is rising in the cool, quiet air.
The thunder of the water washes noises away,
Leaving only perspective and a silent prayer.

{c:Chorus}

Oh, the water falls and the river flows,
Through the high ravine where the wild wind blows.
Like the highs and lows of the days we meet,
Sweeping us up and back to our feet.

{c:Verse 2}

There are seasons when the current slows to glass,
A lazy trickle over moss-grown, ancient stone.
You wait it out and watch the quiet moments pass,
Content to wander through the shadows all alone.

{c:Chorus}

{c:Bridge}

You can't hold the spray, you can't stop the stream,
Let it go and you thought you could command.
Carried along by a strong and steady stream.
Hiding the pace you understand.

{c:Outro}

Down to the basin, calm and clear at last,
Where the roaring fades into a gentle song.
